,"future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"banned","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"banned","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"banned","vintage":"restricted"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"Sol Ring","oracle_id":"6ad8011d-3471-4369-9d68-b264cc027487","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}{C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Twiddle","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","oracle_text":"You may tap or untap target artifact, creature, or land.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2003-07-28","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you create a Beast token, that token can't attack or block during the same combat, even if it gains haste.","oracle_id":"397b9dcf-690a-4a58-8637-bb9baab7cc2f","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players can cast spells after Elder Gargaroth's triggered ability has resolved but before blockers are declared (if it's attacking) or before combat damage is dealt (if it's blocking).","oracle_id":"397b9dcf-690a-4a58-8637-bb9baab7cc2f","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature that is both a Beast and a Bird still only gets one instance of ward {1} from Radagast, Wizard of Wilds's first ability.","oracle_id":"50f144f8-29eb-4af7-9a50-eded3b9c83c2","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Radagast, Wizard of Wilds is a Beast or a Bird, it will have two instances of ward {1}.","oracle_id":"50f144f8-29eb-4af7-9a50-eded3b9c83c2","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Radagast, Wizard of the Wilds's last triggered ability will resolve before the spell that caused it to trigger resolves. It will resolve even if the spell that caused it to trigger is countered or has otherwise left the stack.","oracle_id":"50f144f8-29eb-4af7-9a50-eded3b9c83c2","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cosmogrand Zenith’s ability resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered or otherwise leaves the stack without resolving. Notably, if your second spell is a creature spell and you choose the second mode for Cosmogrand Zenith’s ability, the resulting creature from that spell won’t get a +1/+1 counter.","oracle_id":"e2cd65f6-7cbc-497c-bdc9-698ff17da31e","published_at":"2025-07-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cosmogrand Zenith’s ability will count any spells you’ve cast this turn, which may include Cosmogrand Zenith itself. It doesn’t matter if the other spells resolved, didn’t resolve, were countered, or are still on the stack.","oracle_id":"e2cd65f6-7cbc-497c-bdc9-698ff17da31e","published_at":"2025-07-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Scaretiller becomes tapped while casting a spell or activating an ability, that spell or ability resolves after Scaretiller's triggered ability has resolved.","oracle_id":"e4b32e47-5484-4ee9-bac3-4ba37558a56a","published_at":"2019-08-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Neither mode of Scaretiller's ability counts as playing a land. It can put a land card onto the battlefield even if you've already played your land for the turn, and even if it's not your turn.","oracle_id":"e4b32e47-5484-4ee9-bac3-4ba37558a56a","published_at":"2019-08-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Scaretiller's ability is a triggered ability, not an activated ability. It doesn't allow you to tap it whenever you want; rather, you need some other way of tapping it, such as by attacking.","oracle_id":"e4b32e47-5484-4ee9-bac3-4ba37558a56a","published_at":"2019-08-23","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
